Crossfeed output pair map (K340 firmware fork) for dspi-core.

Why: the owner's K340 amplifier wires one DAC per ear (out0 = R woofer,
out1 = R tweeter, out2 = L woofer, out3 = L tweeter), so crossfeed's fixed
pairs (2p, 2p+1) are the same ear twice. The K340 firmware fork
(Bofr5555/DSPi, branch bofr-main) makes the outputs of each crossfeed pair
configurable; this patch teaches the core about it. Upstream firmware
v1.1.6-beta5 has none of it: its bulk image carries zero in the claimed bytes
(= default pairing) and it STALLs the extension request.

Encoding (firmware crossfeed_map.h): 4 bytes, byte p = pair p; 0x00 = the
default (2p, 2p+1), else (right << 4) | left (0-based output indices). Valid
= every pair p < pairs (4 RP2350 / 2 RP2040) has two distinct stereo outputs
(< 2 * pairs, never the PDM sub), no output is used twice, bytes beyond the
platform's pairs are 0. Firmware stores/reports the map normalized (explicit
default bytes -> 0). Wire format stays V32: the map claims the former
WireCrossfeedParams.reserved2 (crossfeed section offset 12, bulk offset 44).

Hunks:
1. core/src/protocol.rs: the extension channel REQ_EXTENSION (0x00, wValue
   = sub-command, OUT sets / IN gets; 0x00 requested from Weeb Labs as the
   reserved extension opcode) with EXT_LIST, EXT_CROSSFEED_PAIR_MAP (0x0001)
   and EXT_CORE_VREG (0x0002). Until 2026-11-06 the map used opcode 0x02,
   which Weeb Labs' ac3-dts-decode branch also uses.
   OFF_CROSSFEED_PAIR_MAP, CROSSFEED_MAP_PAIRS, crossfeed_map_{pair,
   encode_pair,valid,normalize}; decode_bulk/encode_bulk carry the map;
   tests (wire position, validation incl. the exhaustive 2-pair count).
2. core/src/state.rs: DspState.crossfeed_pair_map ([u8; 4], default zero),
   DspState::crossfeed_pair_count().
3. core/src/commands.rs: set_crossfeed_pair_map (validates, normalizes,
   InvalidArgument without USB traffic for a refused map; state updated only
   after the send succeeds) and fetch_crossfeed_pair_map (Err = unsupported).
4. core/src/presetfile.rs: "pairMap" in the crossfeed block (export always;
   import only when present, invalid -> default); test.
5. core/src/presetdiff.rs: per-pair "Crossfeed pair N outputs" lines.

The C ABI (lib.rs) is unchanged; dspi-ffi wraps the Rust methods.

